**Genuine central completions and spectral projectors.** Fix one spectral multiset $ eta$ and let J in the symmetric Laurent polynomial center be generated by $f(X)-f(q^ eta)$. Symmetric coefficients are central by step 5.1's mixed formula. Each coordinate in C/JC is a root of $\prod_{i\in eta}(t-q^i)$, so this coefficient quotient is finite-dimensional and its geometric points are exactly the permutations of that multiset. All points lie over k. Its radical is the intersection of the corresponding finitely many maximal ideals; the finite-dimensional quotient has nilpotent radical, so its powers are cofinal with the powers of JC. Chinese remainders identify the coefficient completion with $ igoplus_{
u\in\operatorname{Orb}( eta)}k[\![y_1,\ldots,y_d]\!]e(
u)$, with $X_r=q^{
u_r}(1-y_r)$. Step 5.1's affine PBW module then identifies the ACTUAL central completion with the same finite sum of PBW words and formal coefficients, and its spectral projectors are the displayed completed coefficient idempotents. On the KLR side the positive symmetric dot polynomials are central by the equal divided-difference rule and unequal permutation rule. Their ideal has radical $(y_1,\ldots,y_d)$: each $y_r^d$ belongs to that symmetric ideal by the characteristic-polynomial identity, giving cofinal powers explicitly. Step 6.1 therefore gives its actual central completion as the same finite formal PBW module. A finite permutation-stable set with several contents is the finite direct sum of these completions; distinct spectral multisets give comaximal central ideals. Formal multiplication is legitimate: a permutation preserves dot order and each divided difference lowers it by at most one, while the finite PBW crossing lengths give uniform finite order loss. The faithful rational triangular argument continues over the fraction fields of the formal rings. Thus both completions have the coefficient ring assumed in the local formulas, with actual completed spectral projectors, represented by finite polynomial projectors in each nilpotent quotient, and continuous multiplication, independently of any cyclotomic faithfulness assertion.
